ntre los meses del año.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 38 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 1.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 31.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 13.3 to 91.7. December accounts for 13% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 17% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 39,984 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the limit does not mean that any of them were improperly awarded. It could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or the need for multiple smaller contracts to meet specific requirements.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the dates it was awarded. Also, review the contracts to see if multiple contracts were used for the same need, which could indicate a pattern of procurement decisions. Look for any repeated orders from awardee A to assess if they were consistently used for similar services.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["QOxQNU727O9%2BF6L2uCfUWg%3D%3D","Z0MhRtFRzpuLAncw3qdZkA%3D%3D","xfU3LxoPoWseIBJRHQiPkQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}